{"text": "Virtual reality sometimes shortened as VR. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Immerses viewers. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In a simulated three dimensional environment. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Instead of watching a linear series of moving images. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> On a separate and finite two dimensional screen. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The VR viewer wears a special headset. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That makes it appear as if she is surrounded. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> By a digitally animated environment. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Or a space captured in 360 degrees by a specialized camera. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Like a movie. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A VR experience can be curated. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> By technicians and artists. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> They can provide us. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> With engaging and spectacular things to look at. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But virtual reality cannot control. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Exactly when and how we see those things. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For example. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A movie can choose to show us. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A close up detail in a characters expression. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At a particular moment. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And in a precise way. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That conveys specific meaning. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And produces a particular emotional response. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A viewer shown the same thing. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> As part of a VR experience. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Would not necessarily be close enough. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To see the detail. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And could even be looking the other way. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At something else. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At the moment that particular detail emerged.", "alignment": {"characters": ["V", "i", "r", "t", "u", "a", "l", " ", "r", "e", "a", "l", "i", "t", "y", " ", "s", "o", "m", "e", "t", "i", "m", "e", "s", " ", "s", "h", "o", "r", "t", "e", "n", "e", "d", " ", "a", "s", " ", "V", "R", ".", " "